    "scope": "8.h.W adds compare_semantic over explicit ComparisonInputs. Every supplied stored artifact field contract is validated before classification. Existing artifact identities, hashes, presence flags, values and pointers remain visible. Threshold/text, scope/exception/relation/document/verification/code-reference differences retain their structural classes; applicability, product configuration, stored statuses and evidence result/binding/content changes are distinguished. Paired typed ProjectConfigurations compare through the existing semantic projection and also bind their raw declarations. Explicit requirement timing bounds alone enable exact tightened/relaxed/equivalent/incomparable duration observations; policies bind even unchanged input. Missing configuration is not_supplied. Supplied inventory membership deltas do not imply applicability-derived scope, which remains not_evaluated alongside evidence currency. Independent tests cover classes, exact values/identities, configuration and policy binding, invalid inputs, ownership, no writes and fresh-process parity. Existing 277 test files and 9227 IDs remain unchanged. Source adapters, Diff CLI, durable Work, effective profiles, applicability-derived scope, evidence-currentness services and platform/performance acceptance remain open; no release approval is claimed. R classifies additional unstructured domain text and text-bearing namespaced extension values as text_changed without interpreting words, languages, Markdown or numerical claims. Opaque extension keys never inherit Core timing/threshold/status/evidence semantics. Pure numeric/Boolean unknown deltas remain structural field_changed; declared enum, identity and path values keep their existing classes. Iterative value scanning retains complete containers, presence/null distinctions, escaped pointers and exact Unicode bytes. Independent tests cover twenty domain/record text positions, misleading extension names, typed machine values, deep/wide data